#23-25 October 1923. Whether the Hamburg party never got the
#cancellation or acted on its own is still disputed. A party on a war
#footing has given its districts orders that are hard to recall, so the
#event follows the earnest preparation. Spine: reaction.

= Hamburg Rises Alone

Before dawn on 23 October, armed squads of the Hamburg party storm police stations in Barmbek, Schiffbek and the working-class districts by the docks. Whether the courier from Chemnitz never arrived, or the Hamburg leaders chose to act anyway, nobody can yet say. For three days a few hundred men hold barricades against the police and the marines. Nowhere else in Germany does anyone move.

When it is over the dead are counted on both sides, the survivors are hunted through the tenements, and the party in Hamburg is broken for a season. In Berlin the Left calls the fighters heroes betrayed by the Zentrale. The Zentrale calls it a breach of discipline. Both are counting on the same dead.
